# The chance that the answer is yes for each query and document pair.
# Float32, 16 values, one for each pair line, in the order of the lines.
# The rank pooling of llama.cpp reads the last position, applies the class
# head cls.output.weight, and applies a softmax. The first class output is
# the yes value and the second is the no value, and the two add to one.
# The template comes from tokenizer.chat_template.rerank of the model file.
# Backend CPU.
